Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Bluetooth: hci_qca: Drop baud-change VSE; add 3.2 Mbps

Upstream fixes a race where the vendor-specific event (VSE 0x92)
indicating baudrate-change completion may be lost or reordered. The
driver now simply waits a short fixed delay (<=100 ms) after requesting
the speed change and proceeds without relying on the VSE.

Also map 3.2 Mbps (3200000) to the corresponding QCA baud enum so that
platforms using that rate work out of the box.

Based on commits such as:
- "Bluetooth: hci_qca: Drop the wait for baudrate change vendor event"

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@
 enum qca_baudrate {
 	QCA_BAUDRATE_115200 = 0,
 	QCA_BAUDRATE_3M     = 5,
 	QCA_BAUDRATE_3_2M   = 8,
 };

 static u8 qca_get_baudrate_val(unsigned int speed)
 {
 	switch (speed) {
 	case 115200:
 		return QCA_BAUDRATE_115200;
 	case 3000000:
 		return QCA_BAUDRATE_3M;
 	case 3200000:
 		return QCA_BAUDRATE_3_2M;
 	default:
 		return QCA_BAUDRATE_3M;
 	}
 }

@@
 static int qca_set_speed(struct hci_uart *hu, unsigned int speed)
 {
 	/* send vendor speed-change command */
 	int err = qca_send_change_baud(hu, qca_get_baudrate_val(speed));
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
 	/* Do not wait for VSE 0x92; just allow hardware to settle */
 	msleep(100);
 
 	/* bump host UART */
 	host_set_baudrate(hu, speed);
 	return 0;
 }

